{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Play in '''Group C of the [[1990 FIFA World Cup]]''' completed on 20 June 1990.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/90full.html |title=World Cup 1990 |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]] won the group, and advanced to the [[1990 FIFA World Cup knockout stage|second round]], along with [[Costa Rica national football team|Costa Rica]]. [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]] and [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]] failed to advance, with the latter achieving a unique feat in World Cup history by playing three games in a particular World Cup having every game finish with exactly the same scoreline: a 2–1 loss.

